From 78a5ef880282649d4feafffd539e352980d949d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Troy Sargent <troy@paradigm.xyz>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:01:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(certify): require and discharge the loop obligations of
 a registry

solar-verify --emit-lean names, for every obligation past a loop head, the
cutpoint edge it is on (entry, back, exit), what it is for there
(initiation, preservation, termination, body, call, exit) and its outcome,
and lists each unit's loop heads with their clauses and edges.

tools/certify/loopvc.py derives the registry of a function's loop
obligations from that export and checks a committed one against it: the
driver exports the source in step 3b, fails unless the export has exactly
the registry's obligations for the pinned bytecode, and discharges them in
step 6 with solidity-lean's Verify/Discharge, failing on any that is not
proved with clean axioms. test.sh covers each failure, and the driver
failing on an export that lacks one loop obligation. The solidity-lean pin
moves to the commit that adds verify_counter's registry.
