@@ -25,6 +25,13 @@
 # 3. Compiles CERTIFIED/NAME/NAME.sol with -Zemit-lean-stages, checks that the flag leaves the
 #    runtime bytecode as it is, that it is CERTIFIED/NAME/bytecode.hex when that pin exists, and
 #    the manifest's hashes.
+# 3b. When CERTIFIED/NAME/loopvc.json exists (the loop obligations solidity-lean requires of the
+#    contract: per loop head, the initiation, preservation, termination and exit obligations of
+#    its cutpoint edges), solar-verify --dry-run --emit-lean exports this run's source and
+#    tools/certify/loopvc.py checks, before any Lean runs, that the export has exactly those
+#    obligations, each required and with the query the registry pins, for this run's bytecode
+#    (and the committed record's). A loop obligation missing, added, no longer required or
+#    changed fails the run. Step 6 discharges them in the kernel.
 # 4. tools/certify/certify.py writes CERTIFIED/NAME/Proofs: per pair of consecutive stages a
 #    sym_exec proof, their composition from the first lowered MIR to the final EVM IR, and the
 #    assembly walk of the bytecode against the final EVM IR.
@@ -37,6 +44,12 @@
 #    (unproved), never as passing; --require-spec fails on any. When CERTIFIED/NAME/headline exists (lines "MODULE THEOREM": the source-to-bytecode or
 #    spec-to-bytecode theorems solidity-lean states for the contract), builds each MODULE and
 #    audits each THEOREM the same way. --require-headline fails when there is none.
+#    With CERTIFIED/NAME/loopvc.json, solidity-lean's Verify/Discharge/discharge.sh proves step
+#    3b's export in the kernel (lean-smt's reconstruction of cvc5's proof, else vc_valid, each
+#    proof's axioms audited, with its vacuity diagnostic), sandboxed; every registry obligation
+#    must be proved with no axiom but propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound and must not hold
